//! run
//! abort
//! stderr: runtime error: shift count -1 out of range for i64
//! stdout:
//| before
// The twin of 032_shift_of_a_default_typed_constant.ft, one constant apart.
// There the shifted operand is `1`, which fits i32, and the runtime message
// reads i32. Here it is `4294967296`, which does not, so D4.5 gives it i64 and
// the message reads i64. The two tests together are the rule: the same
// expression, the same count, and the type in the message is the only thing
// that moves.
//
// The message is where the default type of an expression that folded to no
// value is visible from outside the compiler. A shift whose count did not fold
// keeps the left operand's own type and leaves the count to the run time
// (D6.2), and the message names that type (toolchain.md 6 item 15).
fn i32 minus_one() {
    return -1;
}

fn i32 main() {
    i32 n = minus_one();
    println("before");
    println(4294967296 << n);
    return 0;
}
